{"name":"Vindaloo","hex":"#ae7579","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vindaloo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blend of chilis, tamarind, ginger, cumin, and mustard seeds, originally from Goa.","A hot curry made with this spice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vindaloo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vindaloo","blocks":[{"text":"Vindaloo is a curry dish known globally in its British form as a staple of curry houses and Indian restaurants, specifically a fiery, spicy dish that can be made with a choice of meats. Vindaloo's name derives from the famous Portuguese Goan dish carne de vinha d'alhos or vindalho, made with pork."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Beef_Vindaloo_-_Chilli_Mama%2C_Chadstone_%283014236693%29.jpg/330px-Beef_Vindaloo_-_Chilli_Mama%2C_Chadstone_%283014236693%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vindaloo"},{"title":"Vindaloo (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Vindaloo\" is the debut single by British band Fat Les, released in 1998 and recorded for the 1998 FIFA World Cup. The music was co-written by Blur bassist Alex James and bassist Guy Pratt. The lyrics were written by comedian Keith Allen. The song was originally written as a parody of football chants, but was adopted as one in its own right and became a classic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b9/Vindaloo_cover.jpg/330px-Vindaloo_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vindaloo_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Toddy_Bottle_and_Glass.jpg/120px-Toddy_Bottle_and_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Toddy_Bottle_and_Glass.jpg/250px-Toddy_Bottle_and_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut